aqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Food, Mexican, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":5},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Food, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Vegetarian","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1}],"text":[{"business_id":"hPd6uMCjNglnOwwHpkY5Tg","review_id":"Hb4-0n5TbK9ABTgIE32tvA","date":"2018-10-18T02:33:51","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9391211271286011,"text_excerpt":"Felipe's is one of my go-to's in the area. If you've ever been to a Moe's, Izzo's or Chipotle, it works very similarly​. You pick what you want (tacos, burrito, quesadilla, salad, etc.) and then you can pick your meat and toppings (I highly recommend Chicken Tinga if you like spicier foods). The one thing that Felipe's has over these other restaurants is just how good and fresh the ingredients are. I can't quite explain it, but to me​,​ it puts Felipe's miles above their competition. Another thing that I love about Felipe's is the atmosphere. It's a great place to hang out​ for drinks and grab a quick bite to eat. The staff are always friendly and know how to joke around, which helps keep..."},{"business_id":"hPd6uMCjNglnOwwHpkY5Tg","review_id":"Ke501mb0u88OOe_X6YL56A","date":"2014-10-11T17:40:09","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9389936923980713,"text_excerpt":"I work in the French Quarter - a few doors down from Felipe's, in fact... And this is HANDS DOWN your tastiest cheapest option for lunch or dinner in the Quarter (provided your willing to deviate from Cajun cuisine). Which is why you'll find so many locals sitting at the bar and chowing on their usual meals. For a taqueria, they have a fairly wide selection - enough variance to keep me from getting bored, as I eat here AT LEAST 3 times a week. The food is always fresh, killer ingredients, excellent selection of meats - my favorites being the 2 types of pork, Al Pastor and shredded carnitas. The quesadillas are my go-to-order now. Delicious, crisp tortilla all for about $7 bucks. The staff..."},{"business_id":"hPd6uMCjNglnOwwHpkY5Tg","review_id":"LeGgGQZjyJfBCa3jPnOXwQ","date":"2013-09-02T23:37:41","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9387877583503723,"text_excerpt":"I really liked this place! It's like chipotle or izzos in that you choose your own fillings (meat veggies etc.), but here everything just seems more authentic and freshly prepared. I had some really awesome fully loaded nachos. Felipe's special (chips, guac, salsa, and queso) is a good deal, but I thought the queso was too buttery. I did like the guac though!"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"hPd6uMCjNglnOwwHpkY5Tg","photo_id":"RQyX1TyOymNOnbVuAxuVMQ","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/RQyX1TyOymNOnbVuAxuVMQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8735733032226562},{"business_id":"hPd6uMCjNglnOwwHpkY5Tg","photo_id":"1ffjLERl5XBvvTNEtWNMrw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/1ffjLERl5XBvvTNEtWNMrw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.85266607